{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794328771,"nonce":"wrgpZfF5pDJRnBdCcd18piy5u7k=","title":"A module's source macro is local to its Rust module unless exported","message":"A russl module's id is a hash of its source and its call site, and its source macro was #[macro_export]ed at the crate root under that id. The same file included under two Rust modules (#[path]) therefore defined the macro twice. Blinc's SDF shaders need that: three tiers (storage, vertex buffer, data texture) compile one source against their own data-access module.\n\nNow the macro is scoped to its Rust module and re-exported with pub(crate). A module that other crates import, and every module it imports, starts with #![export], which keeps the old crate-root export. Breaking for cross-crate importers of 0.2, so it needs a 0.3 release. Test: crates/russl/tests/repeat. The README says so under Modules and reuse.","files":null}]}